What is a Restricted Shell (rbash)?

A restricted shell is just a normal shell (like bash), but started in a restricted mode.
On Linux, this is usually done by running bash as rbash (a symlink).

When in restricted mode, the shell blocks risky features so the user cannot escape their jail.

==============What is sudoers?

The sudoers file is the configuration file that controls who can run what commands as root (or another user) on a Linux/Unix system.

Purpose of sudoers

It defines:

Which users (or groups) can use sudo.

Which commands they are allowed to run.

Whether they need to enter a password or not.

Whether they can run commands as root or as another user

If you want user alice to run all commands as root:

alice ALL=(ALL) ALL


If you want user bob to run systemctl restart nginx without password:

bob ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl restart nginx


Now bob can do:

sudo systemctl restart nginx



